            <ArticleTitle>An unusual presentation of calciphylaxis due to primary hyperparathyroidism.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1351-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 69-year-old woman with calciphylaxis due to primary hyperparathyroidism. A 0.5-g parathyroid adenoma was surgically removed, which resulted in complete recovery of the patient. Review of the literature revealed 7 other cases of calciphylaxis due to primary hyperparathyroidism and showed that prompt surgical removal of the autonomous parathyroid gland lesion results in clinical recovery of calciphylactic skin lesions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
